# 1️⃣ Path Sum

## 📖 Problem

Given a Binary Tree and a target sum, determine whether there exists a root-to-leaf path whose values add up to the target.

Example:

```text
        5
       / \
      4   8
     /   / \
    11  13  4
```

Target:

```text
20
```

Path:

```text
5 → 4 → 11
```

Sum:

```text
5 + 4 + 11 = 20
```

Answer:

```text
true
```

---

## 💡 Approach

At every node:

```text
target -= root->data
```

Then recursively check:

```text
Left Subtree

OR

Right Subtree
```

A valid path must end at a **leaf node**.

---

### C++ Code

```cpp
bool hasPathSum(Node* root, int targetSum)
{
    if(root == NULL)
        return false;

    if(root->left == NULL && root->right == NULL)
        return targetSum == root->data;

    int remaining = targetSum - root->data;

    return hasPathSum(root->left, remaining) ||
           hasPathSum(root->right, remaining);
}
```

### Complexity

```text
Time: O(n)

Space: O(h)
```

