# 2️⃣ Root-to-Leaf Paths

## 📖 Problem

Find all paths from the root to every leaf node.

Example:

```text
        1
       / \
      2   3
     / \
    4   5
```

Output:

```text
1 → 2 → 4
1 → 2 → 5
1 → 3
```

---

## 💡 Approach

Use DFS.

Maintain a current path:

```text
path
```

When a leaf is reached:

```text
store path
```

After recursion:

```text
remove current node
```

This is called **Backtracking**.

---

### C++ Code

```cpp
void solve(Node* root,
           vector<int>& path,
           vector<vector<int>>& result)
{
    if(root == NULL)
        return;

    path.push_back(root->data);

    if(root->left == NULL && root->right == NULL)
    {
        result.push_back(path);
    }
    else
    {
        solve(root->left, path, result);
        solve(root->right, path, result);
    }

    path.pop_back();
}
```

