# 5️⃣ Left View of Binary Tree

## 📖 Definition

The Left View contains the nodes visible when the tree is viewed from the left side.

Example:

```text
          1
        /   \
       2     3
      /       \
     4         5
```

Left View:

```text
1 2 4
```

---

## 💡 BFS Approach

For every level:

```text
take the first node
```

---

### C++ Code

```cpp
vector<int> leftView(Node* root)
{
    vector<int> result;

    if(root == NULL)
        return result;

    queue<Node*> q;
    q.push(root);

    while(!q.empty())
    {
        int size = q.size();

        for(int i = 0; i < size; i++)
        {
            Node* current = q.front();
            q.pop();

            if(i == 0)
                result.push_back(current->data);

            if(current->left)
                q.push(current->left);

            if(current->right)
                q.push(current->right);
        }
    }

    return result;
}
```

