# 6️⃣ Top View of Binary Tree

## 📖 Definition

The Top View contains the nodes visible when the tree is viewed from above.

We assign each node a **horizontal distance** from the root.

```text
          1
        /   \
       2     3
        \
         5
```

Horizontal distances:

```text
        1 → 0
       / \
   2 → -1  3 → +1
       \
        5 → 0
```

Top View:

```text
2 1 3
```

---

## 💡 Approach

Use:

```text
Queue + Map
```

Store:

```text
Horizontal Distance → First Node
```

---

### C++ Code

```cpp
vector<int> topView(Node* root)
{
    vector<int> result;

    if(root == NULL)
        return result;

    map<int, int> mp;
    queue<pair<Node*, int>> q;

    q.push({root, 0});

    while(!q.empty())
    {
        auto [current, hd] = q.front();
        q.pop();

        if(mp.find(hd) == mp.end())
            mp[hd] = current->data;

        if(current->left)
            q.push({current->left, hd - 1});

        if(current->right)
            q.push({current->right, hd + 1});
    }

    for(auto it : mp)
        result.push_back(it.second);

    return result;
}
```

