# 7️⃣ Bottom View of Binary Tree

## 📖 Definition

The Bottom View contains the nodes visible when the tree is viewed from below.

The idea is similar to Top View.

The difference is:

```text
Top View → Keep first node

Bottom View → Keep last node
```

---

## 💡 Approach

Use:

```text
Queue + Map
```

Whenever a node is encountered:

```text
mp[horizontalDistance] = node
```

This overwrites the previous node.

---

### C++ Code

```cpp
vector<int> bottomView(Node* root)
{
    vector<int> result;

    if(root == NULL)
        return result;

    map<int, int> mp;
    queue<pair<Node*, int>> q;

    q.push({root, 0});

    while(!q.empty())
    {
        auto [current, hd] = q.front();
        q.pop();

        mp[hd] = current->data;

        if(current->left)
            q.push({current->left, hd - 1});

        if(current->right)
            q.push({current->right, hd + 1});
    }

    for(auto it : mp)
        result.push_back(it.second);

    return result;
}
```

