# 8️⃣ Zigzag Level Order Traversal

## 📖 Definition

Zigzag traversal visits alternate levels in opposite directions.

Example:

```text
          1
        /   \
       2     3
      / \   / \
     4   5 6   7
```

Normal Level Order:

```text
1
2 3
4 5 6 7
```

Zigzag:

```text
1
3 2
4 5 6 7
```

---

## 💡 Approach

Use BFS.

Maintain a flag:

```text
leftToRight
```

Reverse the current level when required.

---

### C++ Code

```cpp
vector<vector<int>> zigzagLevelOrder(Node* root)
{
    vector<vector<int>> result;

    if(root == NULL)
        return result;

    queue<Node*> q;
    q.push(root);

    bool leftToRight = true;

    while(!q.empty())
    {
        int size = q.size();

        vector<int> level(size);

        for(int i = 0; i < size; i++)
        {
            Node* current = q.front();
            q.pop();

            int index = leftToRight
                        ? i
                        : size - i - 1;

            level[index] = current->data;

            if(current->left)
                q.push(current->left);

            if(current->right)
                q.push(current->right);
        }

        result.push_back(level);

        leftToRight = !leftToRight;
    }

    return result;
}
```

### Complexity

```text
Time: O(n)

Space: O(n)
```

